{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":118711,"duration_api_ms":211504,"num_turns":11,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8e890c20-9498-469a-a150-75d75ee903e4","total_cost_usd":0.73269585,"usage":{"input_tokens":3431,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39772,"cache_read_input_tokens":207032,"output_tokens":4696,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39772,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":189,"outputTokens":11653,"cacheReadInputTokens":902346,"cacheCreationInputTokens":77889,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.24604984999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3431,"outputTokens":4696,"cacheReadInputTokens":207032,"cacheCreationInputTokens":39772,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.48664599999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all five amendments against the current codebase. Two amendments (fr-1-0afb1776 and fr-1-e1c5d607) make factually incorrect claims about the code's current state — the issues they describe have already been fixed. The remaining three identify genuine gaps: missing DO/alkalinity test assertions, missing Monod factor checks in the extreme-scale test, and a real data-integrity bug where deliberate 0.0 substrate area multipliers are silently replaced with kind defaults.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-008e032a","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the test concentration_kinetics_are_volume_independent() asserts TAN/NO2/NO3/DOC/DON per-liter deltas but has zero assertions for DO or alkalinity per-liter deltas. The nitrogen_cycle.rs code has DO budget depletion paths (lines 228-233, 285, 294) and alkalinity debit paths (lines 360-362) that convert between total-mass budgets and concentrations via volume_l. A volume-dependent bug in these paths would go undetected. Adding DO and alkalinity per-liter delta assertions is a legitimate and valuable test coverage improvement."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-7e77d2a4","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified: the primary test (lines 632-681) contains explicit Monod factor verification comparing factors across the two tank sizes, while the extreme-scale test (lines 753-872) completely omits this section. Since Monod factors depend on concentration (S/(S+K)) and the extreme test uses a 1000x volume difference (1L vs 1000L), confirming Monod factor equivalence at these extreme scales strengthens confidence in volume independence. Adding the same Monod factor block (or factoring it into a shared helper) is a reasonable improvement."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-0afb1776","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment claims cargo check -p tank_data fails with E0609 because validation/tests reference removed fields like decomposer_k_doc_mg and aob_k_tan_mg. This is factually incorrect. Reading the validation code at presets.rs:1555-1568 confirms it uses the NEW field names (self.decomposer_k_doc_mg_c_per_l, self.aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l). The old names appear only in TOML test strings, which work correctly via serde aliases on the struct fields (e.g., alias = \"aob_k_tan_mg\" on the aob_k_tan_mg_n_per_l field). There is no E0609 error and the crate builds successfully."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-e1c5d607","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment claims parse_process_params_preset only rewrites legacy plant keys and misses algae keys. This is factually incorrect. Reading presets.rs:1242-1261 confirms that normalize_legacy_process_params_preset() already handles both algae_half_saturation_n_mg_total and algae_half_saturation_p_mg_total, converting them via legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l (divides by 20L reference volume) into the new per-liter fields. Regression tests also exist at lines 2460 and 2497. The normalization path and tests the amendment requests already exist."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-905ce34d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified all four claims: (1) resolved_colonizable_area_factor() at substrate.rs:45 uses `> 0.0`, treating 0.0 as missing and falling back to kind default; (2) refresh_habitat_registry at state.rs:247 writes the fallback back into saved state, making it persistent; (3) substrate preset validation at presets.rs:290-318 only checks `< 0.0`, explicitly allowing 0.0; (4) migrate_v6_to_v7 at save.rs:657-672 hard-codes kind defaults. A user who deliberately sets colonizable_area_factor to 0.0 (to disable colonization on a layer) has that value silently replaced with a nonzero kind default on every refresh and migration. The fix — falling back only when the field is absent or non-finite — is correct and preserves intentional zero values."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f7ebd85d-471b-4572-b3fe-b53bdf22068b"}
